# Renders are reproducible from the seed, the script and the app, so the
# intermediates are not worth versioning — the raw Playwright capture alone is
# ~30MB per run, and it changes on every render.
#
# What IS committed is the finished deliverable: the mp4, its subtitles, the
# YouTube text and the timing manifest. They are the proof the rig works, and
# the mp4 is the thing anybody can watch without running anything.
*
!.gitignore
!*/
*/*
!*/*.mp4
!*/*.srt
!*/*.youtube.txt
!*/*.timeline.json

# ...but not the preview build with captions burned in: it is the same video
# again, and it exists only for checking subtitle timing locally.
*.preview-*.mp4
